place. We define Revenue per Paid Employer as total company revenue in a given period divided by Quarterly Paid Employers in the same period.","context":"Revenue per Paid Employer","section":"KEY OPERATING METRICS AND NON-GAAP FINANCIAL MEASURES","block":333,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001617553-26-000046","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001617553","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1617553/000161755326000046/zip-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/4ae027e9c9f368bdde5767651d93f3730c264ec4cbdf21f964f6148101a5db89.bin","sha256":"4ae027e9c9f368bdde5767651d93f3730c264ec4cbdf21f964f6148101a5db89"}},{"id":"d547ad0abc2cbafc1c0881635fb68c58ff6f90a3ead6c6429cfdc4147b96cfde","quote":"In the quarter ended June 30, 2026, Revenue per Paid Employer decreased when compared to the quarter ended March 31, 2026. We experienced an influx of new and returning Paid Employers, some of which only contributed revenue for a portion of the quarter, driving down Revenue per Paid Employer in the quarter ended June 30, 2026.","context":"We evaluate Revenue per Paid Employer as a key indicator of our efforts to increase value provided to employers in our marketplace. We define Revenue per Paid Employer as total company revenue in a given period divided by Quarterly Paid Employers in the same period.","section":"KEY OPERATING METRICS AND NON-GAAP FINANCIAL MEASURES","block":334,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001617553-26-000046","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001617553","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1617553/000161755326000046/zip-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/4ae027e9c9f368bdde5767651d93f3730c264ec4cbdf21f964f6148101a5db89.bin","sha256":"4ae027e9c9f368bdde5767651d93f3730c264ec4cbdf21f964f6148101a5db89"}},{"id":"eac760a20f6f38899e87e4740961deeff44c4b641528b7bcb5417612122e97c2","quote":"We define Adjusted EBITDA as our net income (loss) before interest expense, gain on debt extinguishment, other income (expense), net, income tax expense (benefit), and depreciation and amortization, adjusted to eliminate stock-based compensation expense. Adjusted EBITDA margin is calculated by dividing Adjusted EBITDA for a period by revenue for the same period.","context":"Adjusted EBITDA and Adjusted EBITDA Margin","section":"KEY OPERATING METRICS AND NON-GAAP FINANCIAL MEASURES","block":338,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001617553-26-000046","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001617553","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1617553/000161755326000046/zip-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/4ae027e9c9f368bdde5767651d93f3730c264ec4cbdf21f964f6148101a5db89.bin","sha256":"4ae027e9c9f368bdde5767651d93f3730c264ec4cbdf21f964f6148101a5db89"}},{"id":"7f14ac1ed215688a61380e10b28855102e73057fb4592e7e26b3e16df0fda747","quote":"We believe Adjusted EBITDA and Adjusted EBITDA margin are helpful to investors, analysts and other interested parties because they can assist in providing a more consistent and comparable overview of our operations across our historical financial periods. In addition, these measures are frequently used by analysts, investors and other interested parties to evaluate and assess performance. Adjusted EBITDA is not intended to be a substitute for any U.S. GAAP financial measure and, as calculated, may not be comparable to other similarly titled measures of performance of other companies in other industries or within the same industry.","context":"We define Adjusted EBITDA as our net income (loss) before interest expense, gain on debt extinguishment, other income (expense), net, income tax expense (benefit), and depreciation and amortization, adjusted to eliminate stock-based compensation expense. Adjusted EBITDA margin is calculated by dividing Adjusted EBITDA for a period by revenue for the same period.","section":"KEY OPERATING METRICS AND NON-GAAP FINANCIAL MEASURES","block":339,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001617553-26-000046","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001617553","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1617553/000161755326000046/zip-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/4ae027e9c9f368bdde5767651d93f3730c264ec4cbdf21f964f6148101a5db89.bin","sha256":"4ae027e9c9f368bdde5767651d93f3730c264ec4cbdf21f964f6148101a5db89"}},{"id":"5cd79710c4d9795f298b3741e7ac403f43f6034d9ff751a56fbc0675dcfb9dc2","quote":"Our Adjusted EBITDA and Adjusted EBITDA margin fluctuate from quarter to quarter depending on a variety of factors including, but not limited to, our investments in research and development, sales and marketing, headcount and our ability to generate revenue.","context":"We believe Adjusted EBITDA and Adjusted EBITDA margin are helpful to investors, analysts and other interested parties because they can assist in providing a more consistent and comparable overview of our operations across our historical financial periods. In addition, these measures are frequently used by analysts, investors and other interested parties to evaluate and assess performance. Adjusted EBITDA is not intended to be a substitute for any U.S. GAAP financial measure and, as calculated, may not be comparable to other similarly titled measures of performance of other companies in other industries or within the same industry.","section":"KEY OPERATING METRICS AND NON-GAAP FINANCIAL MEASURES","block":340,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001617553-26-000046","form":"10-Q",